+// tabs R49-R53: Chromium's horizontal tab strip, with vertical tabs off, in
+// the Stedding window. The owner (2026-10-20): "Tabs look really bad when on
+// top, especially when split." The address row there is a card a gutter
+// below the strip, so the active tab's skirts, drawn to join Chromium's
+// toolbar, ended in the gutter; a split's two halves overlapped, which the
+// dark window's translucent fill drew as a bright bar; and the strip's
+// controls and dividers kept Chromium's Material colours on Stedding's
+// ground. Each test reads what the strip paints or the colours it paints
+// with, in a light and a dark window.
